      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Factor analysis of pain and personality test data obtained from 119 patients with chronic pain syndromes yields seven factors: four composed of personality measures, two involving different psychophysical pain measures, and one sex-related factor. The chief factors, comprising more than 50 percent of the total variance, are \"interpersonal alienation and manipulativeness,\" \"clinical pain intensity\", and \"pain endurance.\""},
